# User unit for the `wm` account (rootless Podman). podman-auto-update pulls a
# new image every night and never deletes the one it replaced; at ~1.4 GB a
# night the disk fills in a few months with nobody there to notice (seen on the
# Mac on 2026-11-20: pulls failed with "no space left on device"). Dangling
# layers are the only thing removed — images in use by a container are kept, so
# auto-update's rollback target is safe.
[Unit]
Description=World Monitor — prune dangling container images

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/podman image prune -f
